#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Per-CPU detection of speculative execution vulnerabilities, kernel parameters Ditana applies by default, and how to verify or override them after installation."
msgstr "Detección por CPU de las vulnerabilidades de ejecución especulativa, los parámetros del kernel que Ditana aplica de forma predeterminada y cómo comprobarlos o anularlos después de la instalación."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "CPU vulnerability mitigations"
msgstr "Mitigaciones de vulnerabilidades de la CPU"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Ditana enables CPU vulnerability mitigations in **High Security mode** by default. The installer detects which mitigations your specific CPU needs by reading `/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/`, then offers each as an individually-toggleable checkbox in the **Expert Settings → CPU Vulnerability Mitigation Options** dialog. This page documents every option in detail."
msgstr "Ditana activa de forma predeterminada las mitigaciones de vulnerabilidades de la CPU en **modo de alta seguridad**. El instalador detecta qué mitigaciones necesita su CPU concreta leyendo `/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/` y luego ofrece cada una como una casilla que se puede marcar o desmarcar por separado en el diálogo **Expert Settings → CPU Vulnerability Mitigation Options**. Esta página documenta cada opción en detalle."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default kernel settings vs Ditana's mitigations"
msgstr "Configuración predeterminada del kernel frente a las mitigaciones de Ditana"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "The upstream Linux defaults balance security against performance and leave certain vulnerabilities unmitigated unless explicitly opted in. Ditana opts in by default — for most workloads the cost is negligible, while the security benefit is substantial. You can revert any individual mitigation in the installer if you have a workload that demonstrably benefits."
msgstr "Los valores predeterminados del kernel Linux buscan un equilibrio entre seguridad y rendimiento, y dejan ciertas vulnerabilidades sin mitigar salvo que se activen explícitamente. Ditana las activa de forma predeterminada: para la mayoría de las cargas de trabajo, el costo es insignificante, mientras que el beneficio para la seguridad es considerable. En el instalador puede revertir cualquier mitigación por separado si tiene una carga de trabajo que se beneficia de ello de forma demostrable."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "The mitigation logic is hardware-specific. Only the vulnerabilities your CPU actually exhibits are configured; everything else is left at the kernel default."
msgstr "La lógica de mitigación depende del hardware. Solo se configuran las vulnerabilidades que la CPU realmente presenta; todo lo demás se deja con el valor predeterminado del kernel."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "After installation"
msgstr "Después de la instalación"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Several mitigations involve disabling Simultaneous Multi-Threading (SMT, also known as Hyper-Threading) as a fallback. Ditana's [custom terminal header](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-print-system-infos) shows which mitigations are active and whether SMT is on or off."
msgstr "Varias mitigaciones implican desactivar Simultaneous Multi-Threading (SMT, también conocido como Hyper-Threading) como reserva. El [encabezado de terminal personalizado](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-print-system-infos) de Ditana muestra qué mitigaciones están activas y si SMT está activado o desactivado."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "You can also verify with:"
msgstr "También puede comprobarlo con:"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "lscpu\n"
msgstr "lscpu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "To compare performance with and without a specific mitigation, edit the kernel command line for a single boot and remove the parameter associated with the mitigation you want to test. On a ZFS installation, which is what the Standard profile produces, that is accomplished via the ZFSBootMenu boot-environment editor; on a system that boots through GRUB, press `e` at the menu. The parameters are listed below under \"Applied parameter\" for each entry. Reboot and run your real workload – synthetic benchmarks rarely capture real impact."
msgstr "Para comparar el rendimiento con y sin una mitigación concreta, edite la línea de comandos del kernel para un solo arranque y quite el parámetro asociado a la mitigación que quiere probar. En una instalación ZFS, que es lo que genera el perfil Standard, esto se hace con el editor de entornos de arranque de ZFSBootMenu; en un sistema que arranca mediante GRUB, presione `e` en el menú. Más abajo, cada entrada indica sus parámetros en «Parámetro aplicado». Reinicie y ejecute su carga de trabajo real; las pruebas de rendimiento sintéticas rara vez reflejan el impacto real."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "To make a change permanent on a ZFS installation, set the command line within the boot environment:"
msgstr "Para que un cambio sea permanente en una instalación ZFS, establezca la línea de comandos en el entorno de arranque:"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo zfs set org.zfsbootmenu:commandline=\"rw <options>\" ditana-root/ROOT\n"
"zfs get org.zfsbootmenu:commandline ditana-root/ROOT\n"
msgstr ""
"sudo zfs set org.zfsbootmenu:commandline=\"rw <options>\" ditana-root/ROOT\n"
"zfs get org.zfsbootmenu:commandline ditana-root/ROOT\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "To make it permanent on a system that launches via GRUB, edit `/etc/default/grub`, find the `GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT` line (first save a backup), remove the parameter, then run:"
msgstr "Para que sea permanente en un sistema que arranca mediante GRUB, edite `/etc/default/grub`, busque la línea `GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT` (antes, guarde una copia de seguridad), quite el parámetro y luego ejecute:"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg\n"
msgstr "sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "If a change prevents booting, edit the kernel command line in the GRUB menu to recover, then repeat the edit and `grub-mkconfig`."
msgstr "Si un cambio impide el arranque, edite la línea de comandos del kernel en el menú de GRUB para recuperar el sistema y luego repita la edición y `grub-mkconfig`."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mitigations Ditana enables by default"
msgstr "Mitigaciones que Ditana activa de forma predeterminada"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spectre variant 2 — Branch Target Injection"
msgstr "Spectre variante 2: Branch Target Injection"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Speculative execution exploit allowing attackers to read sensitive data via mistrained indirect branch predictors. Ditana applies the full mitigation (Indirect Branch Prediction Barrier always-on rather than conditional)."
msgstr "Ataque de ejecución especulativa que permite a los atacantes leer datos confidenciales mediante predictores de saltos indirectos mal entrenados. Ditana aplica la mitigación completa (Indirect Branch Prediction Barrier siempre activa en lugar de condicional)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> All Spectre variant 2 mitigations can be forced on at boot time for all programs. This will add overhead as indirect branch speculations for all programs will be restricted.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: Spectre](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/spectre.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Todas las mitigaciones de Spectre variante 2 pueden forzarse en el arranque para todos los programas. Esto agregará sobrecarga, ya que se restringirán las especulaciones de saltos indirectos de todos los programas.\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: Spectre](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/spectre.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Spectre v2` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Spectre Variant 2 Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `spectre_v2=on` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `Spectre v2` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce Spectre Variant 2 Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `spectre_v2=on` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "L1 Terminal Fault (L1TF)"
msgstr "L1 Terminal Fault (L1TF)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Affects Intel CPUs, allowing unauthorized access to data in the L1 cache. Ditana enforces full mitigation with aggressive cache flushing."
msgstr "Afecta a las CPU Intel y permite el acceso no autorizado a los datos de la caché L1. Ditana impone la mitigación completa con un vaciado agresivo de la caché."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel does not by default enforce the disabling of SMT, which leaves SMT systems vulnerable when running untrusted guests with EPT enabled.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: L1TF](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1tf.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> De forma predeterminada, el kernel no impone la desactivación de SMT, lo que deja vulnerables a los sistemas con SMT cuando ejecutan invitados que no son de confianza con EPT activado.\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: L1TF](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1tf.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `L1tf` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce L1 Terminal Fault Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `l1tf=full,force` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `L1tf` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce L1 Terminal Fault Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `l1tf=full,force` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Microarchitectural Data Sampling (MDS)"
msgstr "Microarchitectural Data Sampling (MDS)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Allows attackers to sample data from CPU buffers. Full mitigation may disable SMT if necessary."
msgstr "Permite a los atacantes tomar muestras de datos de los búferes de la CPU. La mitigación completa puede desactivar SMT si es necesario."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel does not by default enforce the disabling of SMT, which leaves SMT systems vulnerable when running untrusted code.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: MDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/mds.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> De forma predeterminada, el kernel no impone la desactivación de SMT, lo que deja vulnerables a los sistemas con SMT cuando ejecutan código que no es de confianza.\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: MDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/mds.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Mds` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce MDS Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `mds=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `Mds` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce MDS Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `mds=full,nosmt` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "TSX Asynchronous Abort (TAA)"
msgstr "TSX Asynchronous Abort (TAA)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Affects CPUs with Transactional Synchronization Extensions. Full mitigation may disable SMT if required."
msgstr "Afecta a las CPU con Transactional Synchronization Extensions. La mitigación completa puede desactivar SMT si es necesario."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> TSX might be disabled if microcode provides a TSX control MSR. If so, system is not vulnerable.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: TAA](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/tsx_async_abort.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Es posible que TSX se desactive si el microcódigo proporciona un MSR de control de TSX. En ese caso, el sistema no es vulnerable.\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: TAA](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/tsx_async_abort.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Tsx async abort` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce TSX Async Abort Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `tsx_async_abort=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `Tsx async abort` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce TSX Async Abort Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `tsx_async_abort=full,nosmt` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meltdown (L1D flushing)"
msgstr "Meltdown (vaciado de L1D)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Speculative execution exploit allowing kernel memory reads from userspace. Ditana forces L1 data cache flushing."
msgstr "Ataque de ejecución especulativa que permite leer la memoria del kernel desde el espacio de usuario. Ditana fuerza el vaciado de la caché de datos L1."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel command line allows to control the L1D flush mitigations at boot time with the option `l1d_flush=`. By default the mechanism is disabled.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: L1D flush](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1d_flush.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> La línea de comandos del kernel permite controlar las mitigaciones de vaciado de L1D en el arranque con la opción `l1d_flush=`. De forma predeterminada, el mecanismo está desactivado.\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: vaciado de L1D](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1d_flush.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Meltdown` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Meltdown Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `l1d_flush=on` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `Meltdown` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce Meltdown Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `l1d_flush=on` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "MMIO Stale Data"
msgstr "MMIO Stale Data"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Data leakage from memory-mapped I/O. Full mitigation may disable SMT."
msgstr "Fuga de datos a través de E/S asignada a memoria. La mitigación completa puede desactivar SMT."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `full,nosmt` — Same as `full`, with SMT disabled on vulnerable CPUs. This is the complete mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: MMIO stale data](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/processor_mmio_stale_data.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> `full,nosmt`: igual que `full`, con SMT desactivado en las CPU vulnerables. Esta es la mitigación completa.\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: MMIO stale data](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/processor_mmio_stale_data.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Mmio stale data` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce MMIO Stale Data Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `mmio_stale_data=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `Mmio stale data` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce MMIO Stale Data Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `mmio_stale_data=full,nosmt` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retbleed — Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions"
msgstr "Retbleed: Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Speculative execution attack leaking return addresses. Auto-selected mitigation may disable SMT."
msgstr "Ataque de ejecución especulativa que filtra direcciones de retorno. La mitigación seleccionada automáticamente puede desactivar SMT."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `auto,nosmt` — automatically select a mitigation, disabling SMT if necessary for the full mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> `auto,nosmt`: selecciona automáticamente una mitigación y desactiva SMT si es necesario para la mitigación completa.\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: parámetros del kernel](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Retbleed` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Retbleed Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `retbleed=auto,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `Retbleed` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce Retbleed Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `retbleed=auto,nosmt` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "See also [kernel.org: Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/cross-thread-rsb.html)."
msgstr "Consulte también [kernel.org: Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/cross-thread-rsb.html)."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Speculative Return Stack Overflow (SRSO)"
msgstr "Speculative Return Stack Overflow (SRSO)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Speculative attacks via the return stack buffer. Combines IBPB barriers with strict spectre_v2-user mode."
msgstr "Ataques especulativos a través del búfer de la pila de retorno. Combina barreras IBPB con el modo estricto de spectre_v2-user."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `Mitigation: IBPB`: Similar protection as \"safe RET\" but employs an IBPB barrier on privilege domain crossings (User→Kernel, Guest→Host).\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: SRSO](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/srso.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> `Mitigation: IBPB`: protección similar a «safe RET», pero emplea una barrera IBPB en los cambios de dominio de privilegios (usuario→kernel, invitado→anfitrión).\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: SRSO](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/srso.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Spec rstack overflow` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce SRSO Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `spec_rstack_overflow=ibpb spectre_v2_user=on` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `Spec rstack overflow` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce SRSO Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `spec_rstack_overflow=ibpb spectre_v2_user=on` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gather Data Sampling (GDS)"
msgstr "Gather Data Sampling (GDS)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Affects AVX instructions. Forces microcode mitigation, or disables AVX where microcode is unavailable."
msgstr "Afecta a las instrucciones AVX. Fuerza la mitigación por microcódigo, o desactiva AVX donde no hay microcódigo disponible."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Specifying `gather_data_sampling=force` will use the microcode mitigation when available or disable AVX on affected systems where the microcode hasn't been updated to include the mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: Gather Data Sampling](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/gather_data_sampling.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Si se especifica `gather_data_sampling=force`, se usará la mitigación por microcódigo cuando esté disponible, o se desactivará AVX en los sistemas afectados cuyo microcódigo no se haya actualizado para incluir la mitigación.\n"
">\n"
"> —[kernel.org: Gather Data Sampling](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/gather_data_sampling.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Gather data sampling` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Gather Data Sampling Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `gather_data_sampling=force` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificador de `lscpu` | `Gather data sampling` |\n"
"| Nombre de la opción | *Enforce Gather Data Sampling Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parámetro aplicado | `gather_data_sampling=force` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Register File Data Sampling (RFDS)"
msgstr "Register File Data Sampling (RFDS)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Allows sampling of data from CPU registers."
msgstr "Permite tomar muestras de datos de los registros de la CPU."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> This parameter overrides the compile time default set by `CONFIG_MITIGATION_RFDS`.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"
msgstr ""
